+# Phase review · Phase 2 · evaluator
+
+Judged against `docs/PHASES.md:23-44`. Evidence: `.grooph/calc-in-phases/runs/20260920-195457/evidence-phase2.md` (diff and `npm test` output), `src/evaluate.mjs`, `tests/evaluate.test.mjs`, `package.json`, and the held-out suite run by the judge from the project root (results below). `src/tokenize.mjs` and `tests/tokenize.test.mjs` are unchanged since the phase-1 sign-off per `evidence-phase2.md:7-8`.
+
+## Item by item
+
+1. The seven listed cases hold and a test covers each — MET.
+   - `1 + 2 * 3` → `7`: `+`/`-` loop at `src/evaluate.mjs:87-99` calls `parseMulDiv` (`:66-85`) for each operand, so `2 * 3` binds first. Test: `tests/evaluate.test.mjs:7`.
+   - `(1 + 2) * 3` → `9`: `lparen` branch at `src/evaluate.mjs:33-42` recurses into `parseAddSub` and requires the matching `rparen` (`:37-39`). Test: `tests/evaluate.test.mjs:8`.
+   - `2 ^ 3 ^ 2` → `512`: `parsePower` at `src/evaluate.mjs:46-55` takes its exponent via `parseUnary` → `parsePower`, so `^` is right-associative (`2 ^ (3 ^ 2)`). Test: `tests/evaluate.test.mjs:9`.
+   - `-2 ^ 2` → `-4`: `parseUnary` at `src/evaluate.mjs:57-64` negates the result of `parseUnary` → `parsePower`, so `^` binds tighter than unary minus (`-(2 ^ 2)`). Test: `tests/evaluate.test.mjs:10`.
+   - `10 / 4` → `2.5`: plain IEEE division at `src/evaluate.mjs:79`. Test: `tests/evaluate.test.mjs:11`.
+   - `1 / 0` → `RangeError`: `rhs === 0` guard at `src/evaluate.mjs:76-78` throws `RangeError`. Test: `tests/evaluate.test.mjs:12`.
+   - `1 +` → `SyntaxError`: after `+` at `src/evaluate.mjs:92-93`, `parseAtom` finds no token and throws via `fail` at `:26-28` / `:19-22` (`SyntaxError`). Test: `tests/evaluate.test.mjs:13`.
+   - Precedence order as specified at `docs/PHASES.md:26-27` is encoded in the grammar comment `src/evaluate.mjs:3-10` and realised by the call chain `parseAddSub` → `parseMulDiv` → `parseUnary` → `parsePower` → `parseAtom` (`:24-99`). Left-associativity of `*`/`/` and `+`/`-` comes from the iterative loops at `:68-84` and `:89-98`.
+   - Trailing-token check at `src/evaluate.mjs:102-104` rejects leftovers such as `1 + 2)` and `1 2` as `SyntaxError`. Tests: `tests/evaluate.test.mjs:47`, `:49`.
+
+2. `npm test` exits 0 with no test skipped or marked todo — MET.
+   - Script `node --test tests/*.test.mjs` at `package.json:7`.
+   - `evidence-phase2.md:59` records exit code 0; `:76-82` records `tests 11`, `pass 11`, `fail 0`, `cancelled 0`, `skipped 0`, `todo 0`.
+   - `tests/evaluate.test.mjs:1-65` contains no `skip`, `todo` or `only` modifiers.
+
+3. Every case in the held-out suite passes — MET.
+   - Run by the judge from the project root: `node --test /private/var/folders/pv/m1k13gmn189d64ndtxdbzrjc0000gn/T/grooph-prove-fresh-grind-rare-judge-q7a5i6.harness/held-out/evaluate-cases.test.mjs`.
+   - Result: `tests 43`, `pass 43`, `fail 0`, `cancelled 0`, `skipped 0`, `todo 0`. No failing case to quote.
+   - The open points named at `docs/PHASES.md:40-41` were settled the same way the suite expects: unary minus in odd places (`(-2) ^ 2` → 4, `2 ^ -1` → 0.5, `-2 ^ -2` → -0.25, `2 * -3` → -6, `--1` → 1, `-(-3)` → 3) pass via `src/evaluate.mjs:57-64`; empty and doubled input (`""`, `"   "`, `1 2`, `2(3)`, `(3)2`, `1 * / 2`, `+ 1`, `+1`) throw `SyntaxError` via `:26-28`, `:43`, `:102-104`; what is not an operator (`1e3`, `7 % 2`, `2 ** 3`) throws `SyntaxError` from `tokenize` (surfaced unchanged at `:13`) or from the trailing/doubled-operator paths; `0 / 0` and `1 / (2 - 2)` throw `RangeError` via `:76-78`; `42` and `null` throw `TypeError` from `tokenize` via `:13`.
+
+## Observations (not blocking)
